WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:07.750
On lakes, rivers and many Florida state waters, you’ll see a different family: white markers with orange symbols.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.675
They’re regulatory markers, and each shape has a meaning.

3
00:00:11.925 --> 00:00:13.750
Look at the diagram.

4
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.400
An orange diamond means danger: a rock, a shoal, a stump.

5
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.925
The hazard is written inside.

6
00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:24.100
A diamond with a cross in it means keep out.

7
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.575
Swimming areas and dams.

8
00:00:26.825 --> 00:00:32.700
An orange circle means a controlled area: a speed limit, idle speed, or no wake.

9
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.825
In Florida, where will you see those most?

10
00:00:36.825 --> 00:00:38.725
In manatee zones.

11
00:00:38.975 --> 00:00:43.825
And an orange square gives information, like directions or distances.

12
00:00:44.075 --> 00:00:50.400
One more that isn’t orange at all: a white buoy with a blue horizontal band is a mooring buoy.

13
00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.525
So remember the shapes.

14
00:00:52.775 --> 00:00:54.575
Diamond, danger.

15
00:00:54.825 --> 00:00:57.000
Crossed diamond, keep out.

16
00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:59.075
Circle, control.

17
00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:01.200
Square, information.
